# UK design systems and Home Assistant controls

Use the GOV.UK foundations for clear structure, readable content and familiar form controls. Add a pattern from another official system only when it meets the same user need. Where a public-service component does not describe the task, keep the native Home Assistant capability, state meaning and accessible interaction. The page is for maintainers choosing a design basis. The source counts and links are evidence. The decisions are design judgements.

This review maps the **38 documented Home Assistant families** (30 task specifications and 8 additional control/panel families) to specific official sources and local owners. It records **402 direct catalogue entries across 18 indexes from 9 UK systems**, including the Royal Navy Design System identified in the wider slider check. These counts describe the declared source set, not every UK public-sector system. They do not count native adapters, installed packages or certified controls.

The [machine-readable crosswalk](../reference/uk-design-system-crosswalk.json) contains the exact source URLs, retrieval hashes, dates, existing local mappings and the decisions rendered below. The [component organisation review](component-audit.html) still owns shared component families and retained URLs. No existing guide is deprecated because another system uses a different name.

